    55	   it, the code that built that input) to the design choice that produces the whole class. First check whether your
    56	   own last change or load caused it. When several mechanisms stack on the same cases, find them all first.
    57	3. **Step back.** Is it the product's problem, or one the measurement or process made? Read the governing standard
    58	   and the decisions on the topic before writing any rule: the answer is often already written (2026-10-29, after a
    59	   prompt rule dropped evidence the standard keeps: "我们是聊过这个事情的你难道没看文档吗").
    60	4. **The cheapest proof.** Show the change flips the decisive case on real data (a stored input edited and re-run, a
    61	   rule run on a copy of stored data) and count what else it fires or touches. If it does not flip, the cause is
    62	   elsewhere: trace again and build nothing.
    63	5. **The share.** Show what share of the counted class the fix removes. A fix that removes part of it is a patch: say
    64	   so, and do not build it as the fix. A fix that another change subsumes is not built.
    65	
    66	Then converge or stop:
    67	- A mechanism named on its counted class is fixed in the same slice and measured, and the report leads with it. A
    68	  root-caused defect is never parked "for Alex"; a parked fix is an open defect.
    69	- Stop and go to Alex only when the mechanism is not found, or the fix would change the measuring stick or the PRD.
    70	- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.
    71	- A failure called a flake is a defect until traced. Read a failing check to its first differing line before any
    72	  rerun; a passing rerun proves nothing.
    73	- A subagent's or reviewer's report is a lead. Read the code, contract or record it rests on before acting on it or
    74	  recording it, and cite what you read, not the summary (2026-10-30: model readers' 36 "wrong date" flags held 12 material
    75	  errors once each was read against the article, and a counting aid credited a question that was never asked; Alex:
    76	  "那你找到的这些问题验证是真的问题吗？").
    77	- Before any design: ten raw answers read beside their inputs, the whole request read as the model reads it, and, for a
    78	  choice the model made, the model's own account (continue the stored conversation with "which instruction led you
    79	  here, and which two statements did you reject", a cent a case). 2026-10-27: a two-call extraction design with two
    80	  review rounds was written on a count variance whose cause, two contradicting prompt rules, three such probes found in
    81	  minutes.
